    "title": "A counterexample to Takao's self-duality question",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23133607",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-04",
    "description": "<p>For every prime p greater than 3 and every n at least 3, this research note constructs a finite flat commutative group scheme over W(closure of F_p), killed by p and of rank p^(2n), with quasi-supersingular special fiber, such that both the special fiber and its Witt-ring lift fail Cartier self-duality. It gives an explicit negative answer to the higher-rank question following Proposition 2 on page 2479 of Naotake Takao's contribution to Oberwolfach Report 42/2023.</p><p>The proof uses an explicit six-dimensional Dieudonne module, a supersingular elliptic p-torsion filtration, an image-intersection invariant and a finite Honda complement. These are applications of established Dieudonne and finite Honda theory, with the classical cyclic-word framework credited. No first-discovery or first-priority claim is made. The verification supplement includes portable standard-library controls, source references, the bounded priority audit and its access/version limitations.</p><p>This is an unrefereed preprint. AI tools were used extensively in solving, verification, literature research, writing, computation and adversarial review. Those automated reviews are not independent external human peer review; no such human review is claimed.</p>",
